---
// A divider, and a change of register. What follows a line inside a block is an aside about what
// came above it — a caveat, a note on the odds, a reminder — so the paragraphs after it are drawn
// smaller and quieter than the body they qualify.
//
// That smaller text is not this component's to style: Astro scopes a component's CSS to its own
// markup, and a sibling it never rendered is out of reach. The rule lives in the block that owns
// the run of elements (see templates/review/blocks/section.astro), which is the only place where
// "after the line" means anything at all.
---

<hr class="rline" />

<style>
  .rline {
    height: 0;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0.35rem;
    border: 0;
    /* Dashed rather than solid: a solid rule reads as the end of a section, and this is a seam
       inside one. */
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--border-default);
  }
</style>
